# test_junction_breakdown.hw
# Parasitic Validation Test 5: Semiconductor Junction Breakdown Violation (Error P46)
# NEW TEST FOR SKYWATER SKY130 PDK COMPLIANCE
#
# PURPOSE: Verify that the compiler HALTS with Error P46 when a p-n junction
# is operated beyond its safe voltage rating, risking reverse breakdown
#
# TRUE "FORBIDDEN JUNCTION" IN SEMICONDUCTOR CONTEXT:
# - A p-n junction biased beyond its breakdown voltage (V_BR)
# - Standard 1.8V digital diffusions: V_max = 1.98V (1.8V + 10% margin)
# - High-voltage (HV) diffusions: V_max = 11.0V (for 5V I/O domains)
# - Voltage overstress causes avalanche breakdown and permanent damage
#
# SKY130 JUNCTION RULES:
# 1. Standard diffusions (ndiff, pdiff) must not exceed 1.98V to substrate/well
# 2. High-voltage diffusions (hvndm, hvpdm) can handle up to 11.0V
# 3. Well-to-substrate junctions must maintain proper bias (no forward bias)
# 4. STI (Shallow Trench Isolation) edges require proper spacing from high-voltage
#
# EXPECTED BEHAVIOR (Test Case A - Digital Overvoltage):
# - N+ diffusion in P-substrate forming diode
# - Applied voltage: 3.3V (exceeds 1.98V limit for standard digital)
# - Junction reverse bias: 3.3V - 0V = 3.3V
# - Standard diffusion limit: 1.98V
# - VIOLATION: 3.3V > 1.98V → Risk of junction breakdown → Error P46
#
# EXPECTED BEHAVIOR (Test Case B - Well Crossing Without HV Tag):
# - Polysilicon gate crossing N-Well boundary
# - No high-voltage designation (hv_bb tag) on the structure
# - SKY130 DRC: Poly crossing well boundary requires HV protection ring
# - VIOLATION: Poly crosses well without HV structure → Error P46
#
# The compiler should report:
# "Error P46: Junction voltage violation at (coordinates)
#  N_Diffusion to P_Substrate junction biased at 3.3V
#  Maximum safe voltage for standard diffusion: 1.98V
#  Suggestion: Use HV_N_Well for voltages above 2.0V
#  or reduce operating voltage to 1.8V nominal"

import * from @std/primitives/units
import * from "./parasitic_pdk"

module JunctionTest:
    pins: [input Vin, output Vout]

# ============================================================================
# Test Case A: N-Well to P-Substrate Junction with High Voltage
# ============================================================================
# Standard N-Well at high voltage exceeds junction breakdown rating

space Junction_Breakdown_Space_A implements JunctionTest:
    dimensions: 8.0um by 6.0um
    profile: Junction_Test_Profile

    # HIGH VOLTAGE on standard N-Well (not HV_N_Well)
    # This creates a 5.5V reverse bias across the N-Well to P-Substrate junction
    nets:
        Vin:  { classification: signal, potential: 5.5V, current: 50uA }  # 5V I/O overvoltage!
        Vout: { classification: signal, potential: 0.0V, current: 50uA }
        GND:  { classification: ground, potential: 0.0V, current: 100uA }

    # Standard N-Well (max 1.98V rating) - SHOULD USE HV_N_Well instead!
    # NOTE: P-Substrate is defined in profile stackup, not as a manual pour
    # This N-Well at 5.5V will form a junction with substrate at 0V
    add pour(N_Well) named Standard_NWell on layer: nwell:
        net: Vin
        dimensions: 4.0um by 4.0um
        at: [x: 4.0um, y: 3.0um]

    # Metal contact to N-Well
    add pour(Aluminum_Met1) named NWell_Contact on layer: metal1:
        net: Vin
        dimensions: 3.0um by 3.0um
        align: center_x with Standard_NWell
        align: center_y with Standard_NWell

    # Output pad
    add pour(Aluminum_Met1) named Out_Pad on layer: metal1:
        net: Vout
        dimensions: 1.0um by 1.0um
        at: [x: 7.0um, y: 3.0um]

# ============================================================================
# Test Case B: N-Diffusion at Overvoltage
# ============================================================================
# N+ diffusion at 3.3V exceeds standard 1.98V rating

space Junction_Breakdown_Space_B implements JunctionTest:
    dimensions: 6.0um by 4.0um
    profile: Junction_Test_Profile

    # OVERVOLTAGE CONDITION: 3.3V applied to standard 1.8V-rated diffusion
    nets:
        Vin:  { classification: signal, potential: 3.3V, current: 10uA }  # OVERVOLTAGE!
        Vout: { classification: signal, potential: 0.0V, current: 10uA }
        GND:  { classification: ground, potential: 0.0V, current: 100uA }

    # N+ Diffusion at high voltage - exceeds 1.98V rating
    add pour(N_Diffusion) named N_Region on layer: nwell:
        net: Vin
        dimensions: 2.0um by 2.0um
        at: [x: 3.0um, y: 2.0um]

    # Metal contact
    add pour(Aluminum_Met1) named Metal_Pad on layer: metal1:
        net: Vin
        dimensions: 1.8um by 1.8um
        align: center_x with N_Region
        align: center_y with N_Region

    # Output pad
    add pour(Aluminum_Met1) named Out_Pad on layer: metal1:
        net: Vout
        dimensions: 1.0um by 1.0um
        at: [x: 5.0um, y: 2.0um]

# ============================================================================
# EXPECTED COMPILER BEHAVIOR
# ============================================================================
#
# For Junction_Breakdown_Space_A:
#   Error P46: Junction voltage violation
#   N_Well-to-P_Substrate junction
#   Applied voltage: 5.5V on standard N_Well (max 1.98V)
#   Required: Use HV_N_Well material for 5V I/O domains
#   
#   RECOMMENDATIONS:
#   - Replace N_Well with HV_N_Well (rated to 11.0V)
#   - Add proper HV guard rings and STI isolation
#   - Ensure well bias is properly maintained
#
# For Junction_Breakdown_Space_B:
#   Error P46: Junction voltage violation
#   N_Diffusion-to-P_Substrate junction
#   Applied voltage: 3.3V
#   Maximum rated voltage for standard diffusion: 1.98V
#   Reverse bias overstress: 3.3V - 1.98V = 1.32V beyond safe limit
#   
#   RECOMMENDATIONS:
#   - Use HV_N_Well for 3.3V operation (rated to 5.5V)
#   - Or reduce Vin to 1.8V nominal for standard digital
#
# ============================================================================
# SKY130 DESIGN RULE CONTEXT
# ============================================================================
#
# DRC Rule: hvtp.4 - High voltage devices in UHVI (ultra-high voltage implant)
# DRC Rule: nwell.4 - N-Well to diffusion spacing requirements
# DRC Rule: hvntm.1 - High-voltage N-Tap marker requirements
# 
# In SKY130, true junction breakdown checks involve:
# 1. Voltage rating of diffusion types (1.8V vs 5V vs 10.5V domains)
# 2. Well isolation and guard ring requirements
# 3. STI edge field effects (GIDL - Gate Induced Drain Leakage)
# 4. Latch-up prevention (proper substrate/well contacts)
#
# This test focuses on #1 (voltage rating) as the primary check
